{"name":"Lion’s Slumber","hex":"#bb9252","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lion","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A big cat, Panthera leo, native to Africa, India and formerly much of Europe.","A male lion, as opposed to a lioness, which is characterized by having a flowing shaggy mane and taking little part in hunting, which can be done cooperatively."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of the light brown color that resembles the fur of a lion."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lion"},{"term":"slumber","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A very light state of sleep, almost awake.\n\n A very heavy state of sleep.","A very heavy state of sleep."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To be in a very light state of sleep, almost awake.","To be inactive or negligent."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slumber"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lion","blocks":[{"text":"The lion is a large cat of the genus Panthera, currently ranging only in Sub-Saharan Africa and India. It has a muscular, broad-chested body; a short, rounded head; round ears; and a dark, hairy tuft at the tip of its tail. It is sexually dimorphic; adult male lions are larger than females and have a prominent mane that extends from the head to the shoulders and chest."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/020_The_lion_king_Snyggve_in_the_Serengeti_National_Park_Photo_by_Giles_Laurent.jpg/330px-020_The_lion_king_Snyggve_in_the_Serengeti_National_Park_Photo_by_Giles_Laurent.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lion","wikidata":"Q140"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Okonjima_Lioness.jpg/500px-Okonjima_Lioness.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Okonjima_Lioness.jpg/1280px-Okonjima_Lioness.jpg?utm_